// Hand-written types mirroring supabase/migrations/*.sql.
//
// These are NOT generated by `supabase gen types` (no live project is
// linked yet). Once a real Supabase project exists, regenerate with:
//   supabase gen types typescript --project-id <ref> > src/types/database.ts
// and reconcile any drift against this file.
//
// IMPORTANT: every Row/Insert/Update shape below is declared with `type`,
// not `interface`. This is not a style choice — TypeScript's structural
// check for "does this satisfy Record<string, unknown>" (which
// supabase-js's GenericTable constraint relies on) treats `interface`
// declarations as NOT satisfying an index signature, even though a
// structurally identical `type` alias does. Using `interface` here
// silently collapses every table's Insert/Update/Row generics to `never`
// with no error pointing at the cause — see the PR description for the
// full diagnosis. Keep these as `type`.

